From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:11:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] drm/bridge: cdns-dsi: restore PineTab-V packet timings

The PineTab-V mode has short DPI sync and back-porch intervals.  The
generic DPI-to-DSI conversion consequently produces HSA/HBP/HFP packet
lengths of 1/3/152 at the JH7110's rounded 400 MHz lane rate.  The
known-working StarFive kernel and PineTab-V U-Boot both use 52/52/52.

Apply the vendor's pre-alignment values of 52/52/51 and a total of 2587
bytes only to the PineTab-V panel compatible.  The existing four-lane
rate adjustment then extends HFP by one byte, producing the validated
52/52/52 layout without affecting other JH7110 panels.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: André Machado <machaddr@falanet.org>
---
 .../gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-jh7110.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-jh7110.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-jh7110.c
index 404922ddfe7d..1d91c3958f41 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-jh7110.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/cadence/cdns-dsi-jh7110.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/math64.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/syscon.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/reset.h>
 #include <video/videomode.h>
@@ -22,6 +23,12 @@
 #define JH7110_VOUT_SYSCON_LCD_MAP	0x8
 #define JH7110_VOUT_SYSCON_LCD_TO_DSI	BIT(3)
 
+/* Known-good packet timings for the PineTab-V 800x1280 panel. */
+#define JH7110_PINETAB_V_DSI_HSA		52
+#define JH7110_PINETAB_V_DSI_HBP		52
+#define JH7110_PINETAB_V_DSI_HFP		51
+#define JH7110_PINETAB_V_DSI_HTOTAL	2587
+
 static const char * const dsi_resets[] = {
 	"dpi",
 	"rxesc",
@@ -148,6 +155,20 @@ static int cdns_dsi_jh7110_mode_fixup(struct cdns_dsi *dsi,
 	lane_rate = roundup(phy_cfg->hs_clk_rate, JH7110_DPHY_RATE_STEP);
 	phy_cfg->hs_clk_rate = lane_rate;
 
+	/*
+	 * The JH7110 integration cannot derive usable packet blanking for the
+	 * PineTab-V mode from its short DPI sync and back-porch intervals.  Use
+	 * the packet layout validated by the vendor kernel and U-Boot.  HFP is
+	 * extended below when the rounded 400 MHz lane rate requires it.
+	 */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(dsi->output.dev->dev.of_node,
+				    "boe,th101mb31ig002-28a-pinetab-v")) {
+		dsi_cfg->hsa = JH7110_PINETAB_V_DSI_HSA;
+		dsi_cfg->hbp = JH7110_PINETAB_V_DSI_HBP;
+		dsi_cfg->hfp = JH7110_PINETAB_V_DSI_HFP;
+		dsi_cfg->htotal = JH7110_PINETAB_V_DSI_HTOTAL;
+	}
+
 	dpi_htotal = vm->hactive + vm->hfront_porch + vm->hsync_len +
 		     vm->hback_porch;
 	adjusted_htotal = DIV_ROUND_UP_ULL((u64)lane_rate * lanes * dpi_htotal,
